BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Intro to Wheel Throwing with Naomi (6 sessions)  — Sebastopol Ce
 nter For the Arts\, California
DTSTART:20270106T000000
DTEND:20270107T000000
UID:6ebeb2d5af91e807f460faf9830d1dad@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Out of Stock\n      \n    \n\n\n\n\n\nIntro to Wheel Throwing 
 with Naomi (January 2027)\n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n          $290.00
 \n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nWednesdays\, starting January 6th through 
 February 10th (6 sessions) 2:00-5:00pm$250 + $40 Clay Fee (max 10 students
 )Class Description:This course is designed for students who are new to the
  potter’s wheel and eager to discover the fundamentals of wheel throwing
 . With an emphasis on core technique\, each session builds a solid foundat
 ion in the essential skills of centering\, opening\, pulling up walls\, tr
 imming and glazing — the building blocks that every potter returns to ag
 ain and again.Each class begins with a demonstration focused on one or mor
 e of these foundational techniques\, giving students a clear picture of th
 e process before getting their hands in the clay. From there\, students wo
 rk at their own wheels with plenty of time to practice\, explore and devel
 op their feel for the material. The goal is for each person to leave the c
 ourse being able to make a thrown piece — a bowl\, a mug\, a vase — th
 at is genuinely their own\, shaped by their emerging skills and their pers
 onal sense of what they love about pottery.With two teachers in the room\,
  there is ample opportunity for individual attention and hands-on guidance
  at every stage of the process. At the same time\, there is real joy in le
 arning alongside others — watching a classmate pull up a wall for the fi
 rst time\, or seeing a finished glaze come out of the kiln — and that sh
 ared experience is very much a part of what makes this class special.No pr
 ior experience is necessary. All you need is curiosity and a willingness t
 o get a little muddy.About the Instructors: Naomi Fuchs brings a deep lov
 e of clay and a genuine passion for sharing the experience with others to 
 everything she does in the clay room. She believes that each pot is an opp
 ortunity to learn — about the nature of clay\, and about yourself. Naomi
  has been throwing on the wheel for four years\, and in that time the prac
 tice has become a grounding\, peaceful and creative part of her life that 
 has deepened her connection to art and making. Her warm\, encouraging appr
 oach creates a space where beginners feel supported as they find their foo
 ting at the wheel and begin to discover what clay can do in their hands.\n
 \n\n\n\n\n          \n            \n              \n                Add to
  cart
