SUMMARY:Encore Artists: My Beautiful Art Ache (Part 1)  — Sebastopol Cen
 ter For the Arts\, California
DTSTART:20270112T000000
DTEND:20270113T000000
UID:1fd8e05f9b51af2f96cfd8413cd096e5@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Encore Artists: My Beautiful Art Ache\n\n  \n    \n      \n   
      \n          $250.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nEncore Artists: My
  Beautiful Art AcheTuesday Evenings (6 sessions):January 12th\, 19th\, 26t
 h\, February 2nd\, 9th\, and 16th5:30-7:30 pm (2 hours)$250.00 Attendance 
 Price ($240 Registration + $10 Guidebook) Class DescriptionIf you’ve tak
 en classes and workshops and are ready for something deeper\, this course 
 helps you move beyond beginner’s excitement to see yourself as an artist
 \, uncover your deep why\, and build a consistent art practice.Through wee
 kly in-class exercises\, discussions and participatory projects\, along wi
 th at-home art and writing reflection questions\, we look closely at where
  your creative life is calling you to grow across four areas:1. Artistic V
 ision — How do I see myself as an artist?Uncover your "artist’s why"
 —clarifying your curiosity\, themes\, and point of view that anchor your
  commitment to making art.2. Artistic Blueprint — What do I need to lear
 n or practice?Conduct a creative audit of your current skills—drawing\, 
 color\, composition\, and finishing work—and build a clear roadmap for b
 ringing your vision to life. Books\, practice plans and reference material
 s will be discussed. 3. Inner Game — What’s getting in my way? What m
 oves me?Name the patterns and bottlenecks—like perfectionism\, fear\, co
 mparison\, or time—and identify the habits and motivation that keep you 
 creating.4. Inspiration Mapping — Where does my inspiration come from?Id
 entify and map where\, when and how you feel inspired. What feeds your mot
 ivation and interest? From museums\, books\, mentors\, and classes to time
  in nature\, travel\, and everyday life?This class is held in the Creativi
 ty Classroom at the Sebastopol Center for the Arts at 282 South High Stree
 t\, Sebastopol\, CA 95472.About the Teacher: Elizabeth McKoy is a passiona
 te encore artist and visual arts educator with more than 30 years of teach
 ing experience. At 56\, she transitioned from her role as founding artisti
 c director of the award-winning Berkeley Playhouse to directing Artaluma\,
  a nonprofit arts center in Petaluma. Over the past 6 years\, Elizabeth ha
 s taught hundreds of adult visual art classes\, including Sketch to Paint 
 classes and her popular Great Artist's Footsteps hands-on art history seri
 es. Elizabeth is especially interested in what happens beyond the initial 
 excitement of beginning: developing skills\, finding a personal artistic v
 ision\, and building a consistent\, meaningful creative practice. She is a
  passionate acrylic painter who has exhibited her work locally and brings 
 her own experience of returning to art as an Encore Artist into her teachi
 ng. She is happiest helping people discover the artist they always were. L
 earn more about Elizabeth and see her work here.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
 \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n            Register
