SUMMARY:It's Your Song: Songwriting Workshop & Salon — Sebastopol Center
  For the Arts\, California
DTSTART:20270112T000000
DTEND:20270113T000000
UID:31314d1f4bfa2169901fedd24a95fd42@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:It's Your Song: Songwriting Workshop and Salon\n\n  \n    \n  
     \n      from $20.00\n    \n  \n\nMonthly on the Second Tuesday of the 
 Month 6-7pm Songwriting Workshop7-8:30 Song SalonSliding Scale Registratio
 n Fee: $20/25/30Select Date and Registration Fee BelowClass Description: I
 t’s Your Song is a monthly Songwriting Workshop paired with a Song Salon
  that makes learning and honing the craft of songwriting accessible and en
 joyable. The evening opens with a sixty-minute Songwriting Workshop that p
 resents a principle of songwriting craft best practices demonstrated by co
 ncrete examples from popular music. A prompt-driven freewrite activity pro
 vides opportunity to put each highlighted principle into practice. The sec
 ond half of the evening opens into a Song Salon that invites up to eight s
 ongwriters to perform or present a recording of a completed or in-progress
  song for positive\, craft-focused feedback from the workshop presenters. 
 It’s not mandatory to participate in the workshop to perform/present a s
 ong or vice versa. This event is all ages\, but may feature mature themes.
 This class is held in the Fireside Room at the Sebastopol Center for the A
 rts at 282 South High Street\, Sebastopol\, CA 95472.About Supernova Suppo
 rt: Karen Joy Brown and Katie Phillips are two Sonoma County based singer-
 songwriters with over 300 original songs written between them. Their previ
 ous band\, The Bootleg Honeys\, performed multiple years at the Kate Wolf 
 Festival\, Peacetown\, and many other notable Bay Area venues including Gr
 eat American Music Hall and Sweetwater\, opening for artists such as Ruthi
 e Foster\, Albert Lee\, and Robert Earl Keen. They launched Supernova Supp
 ort in 2024\, which includes a podcast\, a bi-monthly "Not So Open Mic: Fo
 r Women & Femmes"\, as well as private coaching\, workshops\, and courses 
 dedicated to breaking through walls of fear and self-doubt around the crea
 tive process with a positive\, craft-based feedback approach founded in th
 e Gateless Writing Method. Karen and Katie are experienced facilitators wi
 th a passion for guiding creatives towards their best work. @supernova_sup
 port\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                  Dates:\n                \n\n\n\n    
                   Select Dates\n                    \nJanuary 12\nFebruary
