 1/17/27)\n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n          $330.00\n        \n     
  \n    \n  \n\nObservational Watercolor: Painting Produce (6 session serie
 s) January 17th\, 24th\, 31st\, February 7th\, 14th and 21st 1:00-4:00pm
 $300.00 + $30.00 Materials Fee = $330.00 About the class: In this six se
 ssion course\, students will learn a unique approach to watercolor\, inten
 ded to address the frustration that many feel with this challenging medium
 . The class will focus on strengthening one’s observational skills\, whi
 le learning a watercolor technique that teaches the artist to see value an
 d color. Throughout the course\, we will work on 3 paintings\, progressin
 g through simpler to more complex forms. With a mix of demonstrations and 
 individualized instruction\, students of all experience levels will develo
 p new skills and have a meaningful creative experience. Our unifying subj
 ect will be seasonal produce - fruits\, vegetables\, and herbs. These subj
 ects are great for beginners and master painters alike\; their organic sha
 pes are forgiving drawing subjects\, but their beauty can be a muse for li
 fe. Instructor Hannah Day is a passionate produce lover and botanical pai
 nter and will share her unique approach to rendering botanicals. This clas
 s will work from life\, practicing observational drawing\, in addition to 
 watercolor technique. With six class sessions\, participants will have th
 e opportunity to develop their skills and build muscle memory with a mediu
 m that often feels like it has a mind of its own. Beginning artists and r
 epeat students are welcome. About the Instructor: Hannah Day received her
  BA in Visual Arts with an emphasis on drawing and printmaking from Univer
 sity of San Diego\, then attended University of Hawaii at Manoa to receive
  her MFA in printmaking. Hannah’s etchings have been internationally sho
 wn and collected\, but her art practice also includes paper cutting\, grap
 hite\, and watercolor. She has taught all ages in many mediums. These days
 \, Hannah primarily teaches watercolor\, observational drawing\, and paper
  cutting. You can view her work at www.hannahdrawstrees.com\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\
